Part of #2457

This enhancement adds additional validator status metadata to the WaitForActivation stream and to the unary ValidatorStatus RPC.

```protobuf
message ValidatorStatusResponse {
  ValidatorStatus status = 1;
  uint64 eth1_deposit_block_number = 2;
  uint64 deposit_inclusion_slot = 3;
  uint64 activation_epoch = 4;
  uint64 position_in_activation_queue = 5;
}
```

| Field | Description |
|-------|------------------|
| eth1_deposit_block_number| The eth1 block number which the deposit log was observed by the beacon chain.  This is zero if no log has been received. |
| deposit_inclusion_slot | The eth2 slot which the deposit was included in a block by a validator. This is zero until included in a block. | 
| activation_epoch | The actual epoch which the validator was considered activated. This is zero until the validator is activated. |
| position_in_activation_queue | The validators position in the activation queue. This field will be non-zero when the validator is eligible for activation, but limited by the activation churn rate. | 


## How to use this feature
A user may request the status of a given validator by their public key. From the given information they can estimate the time to activation.

Scenario 1: Validator is deposited but not yet included in a block.
Estimated activation epoch = approx time to block eth1_follow_distance + eth1_deposit_block_number + deposit voting period +  (position in queue / churn rate).

Scenario 2: Validator's deposit included in a block.
Estimated activation epoch = deposit block slot + voting period + (position in queue / churn rate)

