There are a few areas in the code that loop over arrays and can be parallelised.  This patch adds a new utility function `Scatter` to simplify this process.

Taking one of the interop functions as an example: the function signature is
```
DepositDataFromKeys(privKeys []*bls.SecretKey, pubKeys []*bls.PublicKey) ([]*ethpb.Deposit_Data, [][]byte, error)
```
and a call to it is:
```
items, roots, err := DepositDataFromKeys(privKeys, pubKeys[)
```

A call using `Scatter` would look something like:
```
type depositData struct {
    items []*ethpb.Deposit_Data
    roots [][]byte
}
results, err := mputil.Scatter(len(privKeys), func(offset int, entries int, _ *sync.Mutex) (interface{}, error) {
    items, roots, err := DepositDataFromKeys(privKeys[offset:offset+entries], pubKeys[offset:offset+entries])
    return &depositData{items: items, roots: roots}, err
})
if err != nil {
    return err
}
items := make([]*ethpb.Deposit_Data, len(privKeys))
roots := make([][]byte, len(privKeys))
for _, result := range results {
    copy(items[result.Offset:], result.Extent.(*depositData).items)
    copy(roots[result.Offset:], result.Extent.(*depositData).roots)
}
```

Note this is a relatively complex example because `DepositDataFromKeys` returns multiple results; if the function just returned `([]*ethpb.Deposit_Data, error)` the code would be significantly simpler due to not having to pack and unpack the results:
```
results, err := mputil.Scatter(len(privKeys), func(offset int, entries int, _ *sync.Mutex) (interface{}, error) {
    return DepositDataFromKeys(privKeys[offset:offset+entries], pubKeys[offset:offset+entries])
})
if err != nil {
    return err
}
items := make([]*ethpb.Deposit_Data, len(privKeys))
for _, result := range results {
    copy(items[result.Offset:], result.Extent.([]*ethpb.Deposit_Data))
}
```

I'd be happy to hear any ways of reducing the boilerplate, but I believe this is one of those cases where lack of generics means the reassembling of the results needs to be done by the calling function.

This patch also updates the genesis state creation functions to use this library.  Rationale for doing this is it is something we want to be able to do more quickly as we step up load testing, and it isn't in the path for normal operation of the beacon chain so gives people time to get comfortable with its operation prior to adding it to the beacon chain where it will help.

Speed-up is near-enough linear for the simple case.  `Scatter()` provides a mutex shared across all workers and if this is required then obviously concurrency will decrease due to lock contention.

