Entry fields: `url` required (where requests are sent), `auth_data`/`pubkey` and the per-builder limits optional. An entry without `auth_data` signs the UTF-8 bytes of its `url`; an entry without `pubkey` accepts execution payments from any builder on that channel up to its cap. `default_config` applies to every key, so large operators define builder entries once; `proposer_config` is only for keys that deviate.

Fixes #17513.

## Description

The bad-block check in `validateUnaggregatedAttTopic` was nested inside `if !s.slasherEnabled`, so running with `--slasher` skipped it entirely:

```go
if !s.slasherEnabled {
    if s.hasSeenUnaggregatedAtt(attKey) {
        return pubsub.ValidationIgnore, nil
    }
    // Reject an attestation if it references an invalid block.
    if s.hasBadBlock(...) || s.hasBadBlock(...) || s.hasBadBlock(...) {
        attBadBlockCount.Inc()
        return pubsub.ValidationReject, ...
    }
}
```

An attestation voting for a block already known to be bad then fell through to the later `hasBlockAndState` and `InForkchoice` lookups, failed them, and was saved to the pending queue as `ValidationIgnore` instead of `ValidationReject`. That drops the peer-scoring penalty the spec expects for an attestation that references a bad block, and lets the message accumulate locally.

The dedup check stays behind the `!slasherEnabled` gate; only the bad-block check is hoisted out. The slasher feed at the end of the function is unchanged, so attestations are still routed to the slasher for inspection — they are just no longer allowed to bypass the network-layer rejection on the way.

## Tests

`beacon-chain/sync/validate_beacon_attestation_slasher_test.go` adds a regression test that runs the full gossip validation with `slasherEnabled: true` against an attestation whose `BeaconBlockRoot` is a registered bad block, and asserts the disposition is `ValidationReject`.

Before this change the test fails with `want: 1 (pubsub.ValidationReject), got: 2 (pubsub.ValidationIgnore)`. It passes after. `go test ./beacon-chain/sync/` passes in full.
